Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:56:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat: explain audit records to laypeople from a facts
 digest

Gemini now gets a short facts digest instead of the raw record (about 1.9 KB vs 20 KB for a routed session): hashes, keys, signatures and boilerplate removed, hop ids resolved to names like QR-1->bob, times in UTC, and, for admins only, per-route test counts and the abort reason. Private evidence is never sent. The prompt is a field guide: aborted distribution as a protective stop, policy response vs what actually changed, pooled vs per-route tests, independent probes, p-values in plain odds, with a worked example. The prompt version is part of the saved-explanation key.
